/************************************************************************/
/*                         OGRExpatRealloc()                            */
/************************************************************************/
/**
 * Summary: Reallocates memory for a given pointer to a specified size.
 * 
 * Parameters:
 * ptr (void*): The pointer to the memory block to be reallocated.
 * size (size_t): The new size for the memory block.
 * 
 * Returns: void*: A pointer to the reallocated memory block, or nullptr if allocation fails.
 * 
 * Logic: The function checks if the requested size can be allocated using CanAlloc. If so, it calls realloc to resize the memory block. If allocation fails, it returns nullptr.
 */

