 */

/************************************************************************/
/*                  OGRExpatUnknownEncodingHandler()                    */
/************************************************************************/
/**
 * Summary: Handles unknown encoding by mapping specific names to their corresponding encoding functions.
 * 
 * Parameters:
 * unused_encodingHandlerData (void*): Unused parameter for encoding handler data.
 * name (const XML_Char*): The name of the encoding to handle.
 * info (XML_Encoding*): Pointer to the XML_Encoding structure to fill.
 * 
 * Returns: int: XML_STATUS_OK if successful, or XML_STATUS_ERROR if the encoding is unhandled.
 * 
 * Logic: The function checks the encoding name and fills the info structure with the appropriate mapping using FillWINDOWS1252 or FillISO885915. If the encoding is unrecognized, it logs an error and returns an error status.
 */

